<title>DENMARK: EIB increases 4.0 pct bond issue by 200 mln DKK.</title>
<headline>EIB increases 4.0 pct bond issue by 200 mln DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Investment Bank (EIB) has increased an existing four-percent bond by 200 million Danish crowns ($30.7 million) to a total of one billion crowns, loan arranger Gudme Raaschou said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Lead manager of the issue, maturing in 2003, is Denmarks's BG Bank.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650 ($ = 6.522 Danish Crowns)</p>
